  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a direct relationship between Octyl phenylacetate and SK-VLB through a series of molecular targets. Octyl phenylacetate is identified as a target of Caspase-5, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including (2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-2-[...]-oxane-3,4,5-triol and Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate. All these compounds ultimately target SK-VLB, indicating a hierarchical pathway where Octyl phenylacetate acts as a precursor to a series of intermediates that ultimately engage SK-VLB. This suggests that Octyl phenylacetate may exert its effects through a complex network of molecular interactions, potentially modulating SK-VLB activity in a multi-step process. The consistent scores across the paths further support the notion of a robust, albeit indirect, relationship between Octyl phenylacetate and SK-VLB, highlighting the importance of Caspase-5 as a central mediator in this pathway.",
